# Allowlist for scripts/check_references.py
#
# One entry per line: "<path>: <pointer>", the pointer exactly as written in the
# attribute. An entry covers every occurrence of that pointer in that file.
# Only pointers that are knowingly left open belong here, each explained by the
# comment above it. The checker reports entries that no longer match a problem,
# so remove an entry once its case is fixed.

# --- No. 3, legacy merged edition (not used by the website) -----------------
# The file embeds only music-example1.xml, not score.xml, so its refs (which
# are correct IDs in 3/mattheson/score.xml) cannot resolve; it has no
# <facsimile>, so its @facs cannot resolve either. Fixing it would mean
# restructuring a file that is no longer published.
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #facs-p403
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #facsZone-music-example1
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #facsZone-p4-1
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #m-420
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #m-447
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #m-633
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: #m-956

# --- No. 5, 1731: fourth Presto not encoded -----------------------------------
# "Wo das Presto befindlich" points to all Presto marks. The print has four
# (bars 1, 10, 20 and one after the adagio on p. 327); score.xml encodes only
# presto-000..presto-002. Needs a <tempo xml:id="presto-003"> in the MEI.
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_de.xml: #presto-003

# --- No. 11: the staves of bars 23 and 24 have no IDs --------------------------
# The 1719 text refers to the bass staff of bars 23 and 24 (3rd and 4th bar of
# the second part), but in score.xml their <staff> elements (and everything
# inside them) carry no xml:id, and never did in this repository. The measures
# got their IDs back from the music examples, which point to them. Fix in the
# MEI: in bar 23, staff n="2" xml:id="staff-0000000633397600"; in bar 24,
# staff n="2" xml:id="staff-0000001023194498" (their zones exist already).
encodings/11/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: #staff-0000000633397600
encodings/11/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: #staff-0000001023194498
